Subject: [PATCH] Steady audio RTP timestamps for OPUS only (fix OPUS/WebRTC jitter)
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (branch stable).
Stacks on: 0001-0007. Applies with git apply -p1 / patch -p1 AFTER them.

Audio RTP timestamps were stamped from gettimeofday() at delivery (IMPDeviceSource::
deliverFrame, audio branch), so per-packet RTP timestamp deltas carried capture/scheduling
jitter (measured on the wire: 1252..2164 ticks instead of a constant 1920 for fixed 40ms
OPUS frames @48k clock). WebRTC's NetEQ is intolerant of irregular audio timestamps -> small
stutters. ffmpeg re-encode (clean sample-clock) is smooth -> the payload was fine, only the
timing was wrong.

Fix (OPUS ONLY): for OPUS frames, stamp from a monotonic SAMPLE counter that advances by each
frame's exact audio duration, so the per-packet RTP delta is constant. Re-anchor ONLY on a large
FORWARD wallclock drift (>250ms = a genuine gap: stall / standby-resume / session restart /
forward NTP step); negative drift (drained queue bursts, backward NTP step) is absorbed by the
steady counter and does NOT re-anchor. A 5s-throttled LOG_INFO fires on re-anchor so the field
can confirm it only triggers on real gaps/reconnects, never per-packet.

SCOPE / ISOLATION: the new sample-clock runs ONLY when the encoder format is OPUS. EVERY other
codec (AAC, PCM, G711, ...) takes the UNCHANGED stock timestamp path (the original gettimeofday +
monotonic-floor code, now the `else` branch) -- byte-for-byte identical to stock. This patch does
NOT touch the AudioReframer, the AAC encoder, channel handling, or any audio PAYLOAD. (An earlier
revision of this patch also resized the AAC reframer buffer; that change is REMOVED -- it caused
AAC noise and is unrelated to the OPUS timestamp fix.)

ALL arithmetic stays in the CAPTURE clock (sample_rate); live555's SimpleRTPSink converts the
presentation-time delta to the RTP clock (48000 for OPUS), so a 40ms frame -> +1920 ticks and a
20ms frame -> +960 automatically. IMPDeviceSource never references 48000.

- globals.hpp: AudioFrame gains `uint32_t samples` (per-channel PCM count, default 0).
- AudioWorker.cpp: process_audio_frame sets af.samples = frame_samples (after the clamp). It is
  read ONLY by the OPUS branch in IMPDeviceSource; for non-OPUS frames it is set but unused, so
  the AAC/PCM/G711 data and code paths are unchanged. (No reframer/buffer change.)
- IMPDeviceSource.hpp: audio anchor state (audioAnchorUs / audioSamplesSinceAnchor / audioAnchorRate);
  single-instance because USE_AUDIO_STREAM_REPLICATOR shares one upstream source across clients.
- IMPDeviceSource.cpp: the audio branch gains an `if (format==OPUS) { sample-clock } else { STOCK }`.
  The else block is the original stock code, verbatim. Video branch untouched.

